---
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "March 9, 2026";
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Mini-THON"
  description="Learn how GMHS Mini-THON uses newsletter, analytics, and member-login data on gmhsminithon.org."
>
  <section class="policy-shell">
    <div class="policy-card">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes how gmhsminithon.org collects, uses, and handles
        your information. It covers the public website, newsletter signup, and
        the members-only portal.
      </p>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Newsletter subscriptions.</strong> If you sign up for our
          newsletter, we collect your email address.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Member portal authentication.</strong> When you sign into the
          members portal via Shoo (shoo.dev), we receive and verify your Shoo
          identity token and use your Shoo user ID (<code>pairwise_sub</code>)
          to determine whether your account is approved for member access.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Technical and operational data.</strong> Our hosting
          infrastructure automatically processes standard request metadata and
          performance data necessary to deliver and secure the site.
        </p>
        <p>We do not collect more information than what is described above.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To operate the public website and members portal.</li>
          <li>
            To verify member portal access against an administrator-maintained
            approval list.
          </li>
          <li>To send newsletter updates to subscribers.</li>
          <li>
            To monitor site performance, diagnose issues, and protect against
            misuse.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Members Portal</h2>
        <p>
          The members portal uses <strong>Shoo</strong> (shoo.dev) for
          authentication. After Shoo verifies your identity, this site checks
          your Shoo user ID against a private approval list maintained by GMHS
          Mini-THON administrators. That list may be stored in server
          environment variables and/or a private Google Sheet configured by
          administrators.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your account is not yet approved, the sign-in flow may display
          your Shoo user ID so you can share it with an administrator to
          request access.
        </p>
        <p>
          Upon successful authentication, the site issues a short-lived session
          cookie so you can navigate protected pages without re-authenticating
          on each load.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Service</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Shoo</strong> (shoo.dev)</td>
              <td>Member portal authentication</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>EmailOctopus</strong></td>
              <td>Newsletter subscriptions (when enabled)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Vercel</strong></td>
              <td>Hosting, analytics, and performance monitoring</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Google Sheets</strong></td>
              <td>Administrator-managed member approval list</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          When you interact with these services through this site, their own
          privacy policies and terms of service also apply. We encourage you to
          review those policies directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Data Sharing and Retention</h2>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
        <p>
          We share data only with the service providers listed above, and only
          as necessary to operate the site. Data is retained only for as long
          as it is needed for its stated purpose - such as maintaining the
          member approval list, keeping a newsletter subscription active, or
          retaining short-lived session and diagnostic data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The members portal sets a short-lived session cookie after successful
          sign-in to maintain your authenticated session. Vercel may also use
          service-side telemetry to measure site reliability and performance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have the right to access,
          correct, delete, or restrict certain personal data we hold. You can
          also unsubscribe from newsletter emails at any time using the
          unsubscribe link in any email we send.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are not required to use the members portal or newsletter signup.
          To ask about, update, or request removal of information associated
          with this site, contact us at
          <strong>
            <a href="mailto:hello@gmhsminithon.org">hello@gmhsminithon.org</a>
          </strong>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for the GMHS Mini-THON school community. We do
          not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13
          without appropriate parental or school authorization in compliance
          with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA). If you
          believe a child under 13 has submitted personal information in error,
          contact us at hello@gmhsminithon.org and we will promptly review and
          address it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy to reflect changes to the site or its
          services. Material updates will be noted by a revised "Last updated"
          date at the top of this page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy or your data:</p>
        <p><strong>hello@gmhsminithon.org</strong></p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <p>
        <em
          >This policy explains our current data practices in plain language. It
          is not legal advice. This site may link to third-party services
          outside our control - we are not responsible for their privacy
          practices.</em
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .policy-shell {
    width: min(100%, 900px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .meta,
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--ink-700);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  p,
  ul,
  table {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .divider {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    height: 0;
    margin: 0.25rem 0;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--brand-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }

  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    color: var(--ink-700);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  thead th {
    color: var(--ink-900);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-raised) 85%, var(--brand-sky) 15%);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
</style>
